WEBVTT

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.520
<b>Episode 7   "Kouten"</b>

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:06.520
You two were so lively a few days ago...

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:09.600
Then again, all good things
 must come to an end.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.980
What the heck is wrong with Sanzo and Gojyo?

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.780
I believe it's most likely altitude sickness.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:22.110
It appears that the altitude is already 
around 3,500 meters in this area.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.440
Can't you go a little slower?

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.450
I would appreciate if those who cannot
 even walk would stop giving orders.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.620
I don't feel bad at all.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.560
It's probably pretty bad unless 
you have a very strong constitution.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.530
And let's not forget Sanzo is a normal human.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:39.940
However...

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.460
Jeez, Hakkai!

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:46.970
I'm terribly sorry. It appears that even though
 I'm part demon, I'm reaching my limit, too...

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.600
Seriously?

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:52.250
You must be the Genjo Sanzo party!

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:56.480
To think that bounties from the 
east would come this far west!

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:58.110
Seriously?

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:01.150
<i>They're all pretty helpless like this...</i>

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:03.360
Hakuryu, can you move?

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.540
I'll keep them busy for a while,

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.630
so while I'm doing that, floor it in 
reverse and get as far as you can.

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:14.760
Duck, kid!

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:22.360
Huh?

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:57.790
You okay?

00:02:57.790 --> 00:02:59.210
Yeah, thanks.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:01.920
You guys aren't from around here, are you?

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:04.150
We're on a journey,

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.040
but the guys with me are a bit...

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.410
Did they get altitude sickness?

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:11.110
It's pretty dangerous around here.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.010
With your companions in that state, 
you're asking for trouble.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.170
Hassan!

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:17.420
This guy's robes... Could he be...

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.470
A Sanzo priest?

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:20.920
Yeah, he is.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.860
But isn't he too young?

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:26.460
He could be a beggar 
disguised as Sanzo-sama.

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:30.220
Don't touch me.

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:35.100
We're going to lead them back 
to headquarters... Carefully.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:36.920
Hey, are you sure about this?

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:41.440
We have some medicine that helps with 
altitude sickness back at our temple.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:44.710
More importantly, who are you guys?

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:46.880
The Kouten corps.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:51.120
We're Sharak Sanzo's support squad.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.410
Wow, it's like some secret base.

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:01.790
I can walk.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.270
Are you okay now?

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.030
That medicine really did work quite well.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:10.050
It tasted so bad I wanted 
to rip my tongue out, though.

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:12.070
We've brought them,

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:14.300
Sharak Sanzo.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:24.310
A woman?

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:30.740
San...

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:37.000
I'm Sharak Sanzo, 28th in Arhat.

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:41.000
I'm Genjo Sanzo, 31st in China.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:47.750
Welcome to the west. 
I welcome you, Genjo Sanzo party.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:50.020
Sanzo priests are so...

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:51.250
Don't say it.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.740
So our zealous priests 
are a little overzealous...

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:54.780
A dad joke? Really?

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:59.840
I've pretty much tracked down the 
source of the negative aura.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:02.970
So the Gyumaou resurrection 
experiment is the cause?

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:08.530
Yeah. As the highest ranking priest in the west,

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:11.540
I would prefer to take some soldiers 
and march right into Houtou Castle.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:14.530
But I was strictly ordered 
by Sanbutsushin to stay put

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:19.270
and protect the humans here from the demons.

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.580
And how are things here in the west?

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:24.450
Well, it's exactly how it looks.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.720
A few nights after the incident,

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:30.470
larger towns were attacked by 
the demons and destroyed.

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:35.480
Only small, remote settlements 
managed to avoid that fate.

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:40.980
Even further west from here is a 
dangerous area populated by demons.

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:44.520
The humans live cowering 
in fear of the next attack.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:47.730
They barely leave their settlements.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:51.490
We protect their lives and livelihoods.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:56.000
By patrolling the area,
 we're able to maintain peace and order.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:01.500
The Kouten Scripture I protect is the 
one that governs defense, after all.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:06.750
The journey from Chang'an must've been rough.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:10.890
It's pretty impressive that you 
made it all this way alive.

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:16.390
Does this temple also get attacked
 by demons all too frequently?

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:19.960
This building is protected by an unseen barrier

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:23.900
from the Kouten Scripture, 
so the demons can't come in.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:26.100
The same goes for the surrounding villages.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:31.230
Sharak Sanzo's able to project a barrier 
that big with just her power alone?

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:32.340
That's pretty impressive.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:35.410
Well, she uses mediums, too.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:36.900
Mediums?

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:39.130
It's sort of like dealing with radio waves.

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:42.420
She uses the altar fittings placed 
in each villages as receivers,

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:47.900
and sends out holy power from the
 Kouten Scripture using the bell in this shrine.

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:54.120
Thanks to that, demons aren't able to 
set foot in the settlements around here.

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:56.020
I see.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:59.930
So that's why Sharak Sanzo 
can't leave the area...

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:03.000
There are five Founding Scriptures 
of Heaven and Earth in total.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:09.020
Because my predecessor, Koumyou Sanzo, 
held both the Maten and Seiten Scriptures,

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:12.190
there should've been four Sanzo 
priests in this generation.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:17.810
One of them was devoured 
by a demon in the desert.

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:23.320
The Uten Scripture that was his charge 
is now in the hands of Gyumaou's followers.

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:28.050
I've heard that the Seiten Scripture 
that was stolen when Koumyou Sanzo died

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.470
has also fallen into their hands.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:36.230
Which would mean that there are 
currently three Sanzo priests alive.

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:42.920
But the remaining priest, Ukoku Sanzo 
who possesses the Muten Scripture,

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:46.220
resides in Houtou Castle as a biotechnologist

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:48.980
and is aiding in the Gyumaou 
resurrection project.

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:50.730
What?

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:54.790
The true reason he's aiding 
the demons is unknown,

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:57.490
but one thing is for certain...

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:01.140
He's an enemy.

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:05.490
Which would mean the only scriptures that 
haven't fallen into Gyumaou's grasp are...

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:10.600
The Maten Scripture in my possession 
and your Kouten Scripture.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.620
That's it.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:18.760
It is said that having all five 
Founding Scriptures would be enough power

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.520
to create a new world...

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:22.520
I see.

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:26.770
So the reason that the demons are 
so persistently coming after this scripture

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:29.450
isn't just because they 
want to destroy the barrier

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:31.780
that protects this temple 
and the surrounding villages.

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:35.530
So long as Ukoku Sanzo is on Gyumaou's side,

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:39.500
they'll be able to invoke the power 
of the scriptures they've gathered.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:41.790
Regardless of what Ukoku's true motive is,

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:44.110
we need to protect these, no matter what,

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:46.030
so we do not shame the title of Sanzo.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:48.380
About two years ago,

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:54.930
the Sanbutsushin told me they'd sent the heir
 of the Maten Scripture to subjugate Gyumaou.

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:58.840
A monk ten years my junior,
 the youngest to hold the title...

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:02.600
Not to mention that the Seiten Scripture 
he was supposed to inherit

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:05.390
from his predecessor was stolen by demons...

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:08.820
I was wondering what kind of
 unreliable greenhorn he'd be, but...

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:11.140
Good work.

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:15.400
It appears that you've been on 
one hell of a journey, Genjo.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:20.400
Things are just getting started.

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:23.650
That's...

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:26.720
What's taking Sanzo so long?

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:29.090
I'm sure they've got a lot to talk about.

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:33.540
And I'm sure this is the first time they're 
both facing another high-ranking priest.

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:38.770
Moreover, isn't this the first time our beloved
 Sanzo-sama's been alone with a woman?

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:40.570
Can I go take a peek?

00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:41.250
Don't you dare.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:44.920
Sharak Sanzo has transcended gender.

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:47.090
There's no way that she'd do anything impure...

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:47.600
Now, now...

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:51.090
You know it's when those 
rough-around-the-edges girls

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:53.590
show a bit of cuteness that really gets you.

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:56.150
Well... It's not like I don't 
get what you're saying—

00:09:56.690 --> 00:09:58.990
We can hear you, you shitty, 
pervy water sprite.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:00.690
What the hell are you agreeing for?

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:03.660
Ah, are you done with your meeting?

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:07.730
Does being a high-ranking priest
 obligate you to be high-handed?

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:12.090
Your followers are rather amusing, Genjo.

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:16.000
You can have them if you want, 
but they're less reliable than shit.

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:17.240
What?

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:20.290
I was just thinking how great it is
 that we made it here.

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:20.710
What?

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:23.920
So what do you plan to do now?

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:27.140
I'll give you anything we have that 
might help you on your journey ahead,

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:28.980
be it weapons or food.

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:32.730
Then I'll request some food for 
now and a map of the area.

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:34.010
Hassan.

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:38.110
We have a recent map of the area, 
but it's hard to say how accurate it actually is.

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:42.080
The geography of the region has 
changed because of the incident,

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:45.560
and we haven't been far west since then.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:50.910
That's plenty, although I'm hoping we 
could ask to spend the night here, as well.

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:54.410
Why don't you rest two or three days?

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:58.180
You should probably take plenty of the 
altitude sickness medicine with you, as well.

00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:00.810
You want me to drink more of that crap?

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:02.390
Is it that gross?

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:03.900
You wanna try some?

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:10.100
<b>Stiff</b>

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:08.530
Even Hakkai's smile froze for five seconds
 after he just had a sip of it.

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:10.100
Yeah, I'm good.

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:13.000
No, we'll be happy to take some.

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:16.230
If we're unable to fight again, 
we'll be sitting ducks for sure.

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:17.650
Sharak-sama!

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:22.280
There are flames rising up from Osk Village,
 south-southeast from here!

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:23.910
A fire?

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:26.900
But there's something 
suspicious around the flames.

00:11:27.430 --> 00:11:30.780
It's possible that the demons 
started the fire from the outside.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:34.040
Hey, out of the way.

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:37.300
Could we ask for one of you to lead the way?

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:39.170
All right. I'll—

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:42.160
Sharak!

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:42.760
Go.

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:46.070
Sanzo, get in the back.

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:48.810
Poor little Sanzo-sama.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:53.400
The road looks a bit rough, 
so I can't guarantee your safety.

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:57.020
I'm not too familiar with 
either guarantees or safety.

00:11:57.370 --> 00:11:58.880
That's good to hear.

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:02.270
Damn her...

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:04.020
Come on, let's go!

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:15.180
How dare they put up this stupid barrier!

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:18.990
I guess we'll just have to 
barbecue them from the inside—

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:20.160
Huh?

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:25.430
You've got some nerve 
coming into my territory.

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:28.430
Hope you're prepared for the 
consequences, you little worms.

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:32.130
Goodness, I can actually hear the theme from
 <i>Battles Without Honor and Humanity</i>.

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:35.770
A-Apparently Sharak Sanzo 
herself came to greet us...

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:37.650
H-Hey, that guy...

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:40.270
Could he actually be the 
bounty from the east...

00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:42.810
Genjo Sanzo?!

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:46.780
Well, aren't you quite the celebrity, Genjo?

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:47.800
Sadly.

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:52.630
Who cares? We've got two 
Sanzos and two scriptures.

00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:55.830
We're about to get our money 
and eat flesh that'll give us eternal life.

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:56.900
How lucky can we get?!

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:57.790
Well, then...

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:00.950
You just keep chasing that 
pipe dream right into hell!

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:07.130
Hey, now... It's gonna get ugly 
if you forget about us over here.

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:15.100
Sharak, use this opportunity 
to save the villagers inside.

00:13:15.340 --> 00:13:16.850
I'll leave this to you.

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:17.640
Damn it...

00:13:18.970 --> 00:13:23.400
Am I not enough Sanzo for you?
 Talk about picky.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:28.410
Are you all right?

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:29.580
Sharak-sama!

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:31.160
Sanzo-sama is here!

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:33.540
Everyone, head out of the village!

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:35.790
The demons are being taken 
care of as we speak.

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:39.160
I ask that the men carry those 
who are old or can't walk.

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:43.810
Don't cry. Just concentrate 
on getting out of here alive.

00:13:43.810 --> 00:13:44.970
Sharak-sama,

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:46.880
there are so many wounded...

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:48.800
Is my squad not here yet?

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:52.720
Who else can't move? Hurry!

00:13:53.630 --> 00:13:55.370
Sorry, there's one more over here.

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:56.300
Got it!

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:59.420
Let's go. I'll lead the way.

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:01.950
Make sure you hold on to the children 
and cover them as you move.

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:02.970
R-Right...

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:08.060
The villagers are already heading this way.

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:10.310
There's no end to this.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.280
Take care of them in one blow, Sanzo.

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:14.830
Don't order me around.

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:19.460
Om manihatsumeiun...

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:21.810
Makai Tenjo!

00:14:22.610 --> 00:14:24.770
Ra sati unu is!

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:40.090
We've managed to evacuate all of the 
victims who lost their homes in the blaze.

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:43.140
We've also put the fire completely out,

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:45.570
so we will start repairs in the morning.

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:47.630
Good work. I'm counting on you all.

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:52.760
I told you to rest, yet I ended up 
putting all of you to work.

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:54.970
We're all in the same boat.

00:14:55.730 --> 00:14:57.780
Business as usual.

00:14:58.090 --> 00:14:59.540
It's true...

00:15:00.470 --> 00:15:06.080
that with my power, I'm limited to just 
protecting the villages around here.

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:08.260
It seems they've caught onto that.

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:11.090
If it were just a quick technique,
 it'd be one thing,

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:14.130
but I'm sure you're pushed to the 
limits if you're consistently

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:15.640
invoking the power of the scripture.

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:20.640
I would like to set more receivers 
around the area and spread the barrier

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:23.280
through this whole territory,

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:24.390
but...

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:26.660
In the end,

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:30.650
you're concerned that would feed into people 
denying that demons exist at all.

00:15:32.630 --> 00:15:35.400
If this were natural selection, it'd be one thing...

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:38.230
But since this situation is entirely man-made,

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:43.900
I just can't accept that one side being 
completely eliminated is what's best.

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:46.270
I'm definitely relieved

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:49.570
that the last remaining high-ranking 
priest is a decent person.

00:15:49.570 --> 00:15:50.790
Right, Sanzo?

00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:53.430
Why are you asking me?

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:57.200
Or, really, isn't it a bit confusing 
that there are two Sanzos?

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:59.310
It's basically like a job title, right?

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:04.970
Well, it's sort of like we've been calling 
him department chief or section chief.

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:07.270
At least call me president or chairman.

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:11.270
It'd be a bit awkward to
 start calling you "Genjo" now.

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:12.880
So what about Gen-san?

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:14.070
Lame!

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:18.260
Gen-san is going a bit too far, 
so how about Gen-tan or Gen-pyon?

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:21.280
Do you want me to split 
all three of your heads open?

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:23.910
Honestly...

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:27.530
Your followers are really something, Genjo.

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:29.540
Unfortunately.

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:31.460
Pardon.

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:36.730
We're about to hand out rice to the victims, 
but would you like to join us for dinner?

00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:38.050
Yup! I'll go!

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:42.160
If there's anything I can help with, 
please let me know.

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:44.200
Don't trouble yourself. You're our guests.

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:47.060
Once I'm done, let's have a drink.
 I've got some good stuff.

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:50.050
Sharak, do you have a moment?

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:48.410
Really?

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:50.070
I'm dry as a bone!

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:51.570
Do you guys have cola, too?

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:54.380
Well, we have been only drinking 
butter tea lately...

00:16:59.070 --> 00:17:03.080
What were you talking to Genjo Sanzo
 about earlier this evening?

00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:05.100
The scriptures.

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:07.100
You know that by combining 
the individual powers

00:17:07.100 --> 00:17:09.660
of the Founding Scriptures 
of Heaven and Earth,

00:17:09.660 --> 00:17:12.600
you can create new techniques, right?

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:15.790
Sort of... It's not like I've seen it done.

00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:17.520
Neither have I.

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:20.980
In order to prevent unknown powers 
being invoked accidentally,

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:24.090
the Sanzo priests are spread 
out throughout the land.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:28.160
Earlier today, we coincidentally happened
 to invoke ours at the same time,

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:30.600
though we kept somewhat of a distance...

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:33.090
So you realized it, as well?

00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:37.350
Yeah. It was subtle, but it was as though 
our scriptures resonated with each other.

00:17:37.580 --> 00:17:40.170
The Maten Scripture and 
the Kouten Scripture...

00:17:40.170 --> 00:17:42.360
I have no idea what kind of techniques

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:45.530
could come to be from their intertwining.

00:17:45.880 --> 00:17:48.270
The powers of the Founding Scriptures
 of Heaven and Earth

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:51.120
are not always guaranteed to work positively.

00:17:51.120 --> 00:17:55.770
Meaning we should follow tradition
 and avoid invoking them at the same time.

00:17:55.770 --> 00:17:57.130
It appears so.

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:02.260
Although, I do sort of want 
to see what'd happen.

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:03.650
What?

00:18:03.650 --> 00:18:06.260
Nothing. You just said 
what I was thinking first.

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:09.970
You said you were going to go help restore 
the village in the morning, right?

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:13.640
If you don't have enough men, I'll...

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:19.600
Move.

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:22.560
What if I say no?

00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:28.570
I've told you time and time again 
not to look at me as a woman.

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:31.950
And I've told you my feelings over and over.

00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:35.550
I don't care if you're a 
high-ranking priest or a demon.

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:37.880
You're so strange.

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:44.910
So you like Sharak?

00:18:45.760 --> 00:18:51.150
Oh, sorry. I got lost looking for the 
bathroom and heard a familiar voice, so...

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:54.700
I-I see... The bathroom is just...

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:56.690
Hey.

00:18:57.680 --> 00:19:02.320
If you're worried about Sharak and our Sanzo,
 I don't think they're like that.

00:19:03.090 --> 00:19:04.990
"Like that"? You...

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:09.020
I've been with Sanzo since way before 
we started on this journey.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:13.150
And we're definitely his friends, but...

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:19.510
Sanzo priests are extremely alone at times...

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:22.240
I think the same goes for Sharak.

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:27.260
I know that Sanzo hasn't met any other 
high-ranking priests like himself

00:19:27.260 --> 00:19:33.410
who've gone through the same pain and 
hardships and could understand all of that...

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:37.660
So I'm really glad we came here.

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:41.650
Genjo Sanzo has some good followers.

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:48.220
I've known Sharak ever since she was training,
 and I've been in love with her since then.

00:19:49.070 --> 00:19:52.430
Right now, I thought I'd be satisfied 
with just wanting to protect her

00:19:52.430 --> 00:19:54.990
in any way possible because 
she's a high-ranking priest...

00:19:55.890 --> 00:20:03.050
But in the end, as a man, I got jealous of 
the one person she can actually talk to.

00:20:03.540 --> 00:20:05.150
I'm a failure as a follower.

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:11.670
Goku sure is taking a long time. 
I need to take a piss, too.

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:15.800
Well, this building is built in a unique way,
 so he might've gotten lost.

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:18.060
Well, guess I'll just have to go look for him...

00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:21.810
Are you all right?

00:20:21.810 --> 00:20:23.080
What the...

00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:26.070
It's been a while since the last time I drank.

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:27.360
Gojyo...

00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:30.610
Huh? What's up?

00:20:31.010 --> 00:20:33.380
No, it's nothing. Don't mind me.

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:35.290
<i>When did that...</i>

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:42.300
Don't hate me...

00:20:42.810 --> 00:20:45.310
I didn't have any other choice.

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:49.930
Huh?

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:50.550
What's wrong?

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:54.780
The Kouten Scripture's barrier...

00:20:55.050 --> 00:20:56.230
has been broken?!

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:02.940
It begins.

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:40.000
<b>Episode 8
 "Barrier"</b>

00:22:35.450 --> 00:22:37.880
Episode 8, "Barrier."

00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:39.740
Watch without fail.

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:43.000
<b>Lettering: Hoshi Soichiro</b>

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:43.000
<b>Ura Sai</b>

00:22:40.650 --> 00:22:42.660
Ura Sai.

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:58.770
<b>Ice</b>

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:53.270
Ow!

00:22:56.350 --> 00:22:58.780
Damn, that hurts!

00:22:58.770 --> 00:22:59.400
<b>Ice</b>

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:03.830
Ow!

00:23:03.830 --> 00:23:05.140
You're late!

00:23:05.140 --> 00:23:06.870
Off we go!
